 "title": "How to Earn Respect Back at Work",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "This video explains how to deal with coworkers who disrespect you by addressing it calmly the first time, and then creating distance if the behavior continues. The main lesson is that you cannot cut off coworkers, but you can control your access and show them the real cost of disrespect.",
 "key_points": [
  "Address the disrespect calmly the very first time it happens, explain it clearly, and give them a chance to fix it.",
  "If the disrespect continues after you have already given them a chance, do not explain it again and do not have another conversation about your boundaries.",
  "Control your access: stop sharing ideas before meetings, take all conversations over email to have a record, and stop doing them favors after hours.",
  "Keep interactions polite, professional, and minimal.",
  "Distance is the answer to someone who keeps disrespecting you, so they realize there is a real cost to their behavior."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Ritesh Giri. Text / caption: not every workplace problem needs a conversation. Transcript: This is the only way to gain your respect back from coworkers who keep disrespecting you. If a coworker at the workplace disrespects you, maybe they talk down to you in a meeting, maybe they dismiss your work, maybe they interrupt you all the time, maybe they don't respect your boundaries. Then the first time, talk to them calmly, explain them calmly, and give them a chance to fix. Tell them clearly so that they don't have doubts. Hey, don't talk to me like that. I don't take calls after 6:00 p.m. But if you have already done that conversation and you have already given them a chance and they still keep repeating that behavior, then don't give them another chance, don't have that conversation again. Another conversation with them looks like you are explaining your boundary, and for them from their perspective, it looks like the cost of breaking your boundary or cost of disrespecting you is just another explanation which they are happy to pay. See, I know it is not possible to walk away from a coworker or it is not possible to walk away from your boss. You can't do that, you can't ignore them. But you can definitely control the access. Kitna access aap unko de rahe ho yeh aap control kar sakte ho. You stop sharing your ideas with them before the meeting. You take all your conversations over an email from now on because you want a record of everything. You stop doing them favors after hours. They still get the work done by you, but they don't get you. You can keep it polite, professional, and minimal. Kisi se panga lene ki zarurat nahi hai. Toh agli baar yeh yaad rakhna, distance. Distance is the answer to someone who keeps disrespecting you. They need to realize there's a real cost if they keep disrespecting you. Thank you so much and don't forget to follow for more workplace and leadership talks.",
